(1)    1/    BAA2 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1)    2/    BAA2 : =$1                  OPL_S1_Compatibility: equ 1
(1)    3/    BAA2 :                     ; If 1, adds compatibility for the Sonic 1 objpos layout without needing any
(1)    4/    BAA2 :                     ; further adjustments. This will account for the following limitations:
(1)    5/    BAA2 :                     ; * Sonic 3 introduces one extra bit to the upper portion of the second word,
(1)    6/    BAA2 :                     ;   which is called the "y-check skip" flag. This pushes the x-flip/y-flip
(1)    7/    BAA2 :                     ;   flags one bit further to the right, so it has to be accounted for.
(1)    8/    BAA2 :                     ; * Sonic 3 can place object IDs up to $FF in the level. Sonic 1 can only go
(1)    9/    BAA2 :                     ;   up to a maximum of $7F, as the MSB is reserved for the (now-unused)
(1)   10/    BAA2 :                     ;   remember-state flag. Even though it's no longer necessary, we need to
(1)   11/    BAA2 :                     ;   keep the limit or else objects would load with invalid IDs, unless
(1)   12/    BAA2 :                     ;   adjusted to never set the remember-state flag in the objpos layout.
(1)   13/    BAA2 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1)   14/    BAA2 :                     
(1)   15/    BAA2 :                     ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1)   16/    BAA2 :                     ; Objects Manager
