(1)   39/   12D1E :                     		; Each byte in v_time is treated individually in the format "00 0M SS FF", and it's updated right-to-left:
(1)   40/   12D1E :                     		;   FF (v_timecent) = frame counter for one second (increments seconds after crossing 60 and resets to 00, used internally only)
(1)   41/   12D1E :                     		;   SS (v_timesec)  = seconds (increments minutes after crossing 60 and resets to 00)
(1)   42/   12D1E :                     		;   0M (v_timemin)  = minutes (can't ever go above 9 due to time overs, so high nibble is unused)
(1)   43/   12D1E :                     		;   00              = unused (although it could be used for a hypothetical "hours" counter)
(1)   44/   12D1E :                     
